<!--
    Paste this snippet inside the <inbound> section of a policy. In an API-level policy, put it
    after <base />. The All APIs (global) policy has no <base /> - just add it inside <inbound>.

    Where to put it - it must be at a scope where Application Insights logging is enabled:
      - "All APIs" policy -> every LLM API gets tracked (simplest).
      - A specific API's policy -> only that API (i.e. only that PTU) gets tracked.

    Requirements (full checklist in README.md in this folder):
      - The API must be an LLM API in OpenAI Chat Completions / Responses format (or Anthropic /
        Vertex AI); the policy reads token counts from the response's "usage" section.
      - Application Insights logging enabled on the API, custom metrics with dimensions enabled in
        Application Insights, and "metrics": true set (Enable-ApimAppInsightsMetrics.ps1).

    What it does:
      Emits token-usage metrics (Total / Prompt / Completion Tokens) tagged with the APIM
      subscription and API that made each call. Azure Monitor platform metrics can't split by
      subscription, so this is the built-in way to see which subscription consumes which PTU.

    "namespace" is just a label (it's how the metrics are grouped in Application Insights' Metrics
    explorer); rename it if you like. Max 5 dimensions per policy; this uses 2.
-->
<llm-emit-token-metric namespace="PtuSubscriptionUsage">
    <dimension name="Subscription ID" />
    <dimension name="API ID" />
</llm-emit-token-metric>
